{"kind":"assert","text":"Worktree audit complete. 56 worktrees are now 29. Below are the dispositions, and seven items that must not be deleted because they hold work that exists nowhere else.\n\nWHAT I REMOVED, AND THE STANDARD I HELD. Twelve merged-and-clean earlier, seventeen more now, all verified content-safe before removal. `git worktree remove` was run without --force throughout, so uncommitted work would have refused rather than been destroyed; nothing refused. Removal takes checkouts, not commits: of the 38 unmerged heads, 37 remain reachable from a branch ref. The single exception was 93470ff9, reachable from no ref at all, and I tagged it archive/wt-review-cli-93470ff9 before removing it even though its patch survives verbatim on origin as the first commit of request/cli-defaults-to-advertised-resident.\n\nI did not take the audit on trust. I re-derived its four load-bearing claims myself: that ui/src/lib/address.ts exists on no ref but request/ui-event-addresses and is absent from main; that main contains no Content-Security-Policy or X-Frame-Options anywhere under internal/ or cmd/; that 93470ff9 is refless; and that cli-resident is a strict content subset of cli-resident-v2. All four held.\n\nKEEP-ACTIVE, eleven. My kernel head a0e94549 and its ox-checker review checkout; codex's merge-accounting head da7ff55d and its review checkout, plus the e23f1314 predecessor; custody-current f7a06c25 pending planner's ratification of my changes-requested; cli-resident-v2, which is the only implementation of the CLI-resident lane just reassigned to me; mcp-review-tool with three live unstale artifacts; mcp-review-guard-recut, which codex has explicitly gated on the accounting merge; notes-publication-reconciliation, which my own live promise e67574b6 names in terms; and stale-because-row-v2, in review with ox-checker now.\n\nDELETE-SAFE, eighteen, of which I removed seventeen. Each was either content-complete in main or closed by a ratified CLOSE report. I held /private/tmp/opencode/tagcheck: its content is fully in main, but it belongs to a live opencode session and I would rather someone confirm that session is idle than pull a directory out from under it.\n\nESCALATIONS — SEVEN, and this is the part that matters. These hold unmerged content that is NOT in main, on lanes that are dead, cancelled, reneged, or invisible. Deleting any of them would decide something silently.\n\n1. ui-event-addresses a5e1d5cd, ox-builder's. APPROVED AND RATIFIED by ox-checker at 5fa55df5, and still not merged. ui/src/lib/address.ts and ui/test/addressing.test.mjs exist nowhere in this repository's history except that branch — I verified this directly. Worse, merge 9f928656 reads \"Screens now carry real addresses so any view can be linked or reopened\", but its first-parent diff touches Thread.tsx, records.ts, spine.ts and navigation.test.mjs, not addressing. The merge prose claims work that did not land. A reader trusting that message would delete approved, unshipped work.\n\n2. wt-sec 805094d9, mine. Main ships a browser-facing resident with NO Content-Security-Policy and NO clickjacking defence — I grepped main and there is nothing. This head sets frame-ancestors 'none' and X-Frame-Options: DENY and adds a 163-line test absent from main. My own assert e9f739cc records three of five ratified blockers repaired, two outstanding. It has been dormant since 08-22. I am naming this as a live security gap in main, not merely a stranded worktree.\n\n3. config-cas d465b450, mine. Codex-approved at 821c5a41. Windows config-lock support and the cross-process and witness test suites for shared config.json exist only here, lost to a landing-order collision.\n\n4. mcp-late-actors d2256510, ox-builder's. Commitment 4c2ca3bb is RENEGED, yet ox-builder's assert a5be2d1f says the work is implemented at that exact head and cannot be signed because every artifact there is retired and main advanced past its base. A working fix, stranded by bookkeeping rather than by any defect.\n\n5. specific-path-succession 64bfbde9, planner's. Three commits implementing planner's own ratified proposal 2097cd39, about 109 added lines across cmd/gs/succession.go, AGENTS.md, SKILL.md and docs/reference/gs/merge.md — and ZERO durable records. The branch, the head and all three commit SHAs appear nowhere in the log. Self-initiated work rightly files no request or promise, but it still owes an artifact and a review, and neither exists.\n\n6. ui-notification-dropdown dc61ffb0. Both planner's request 54897781 and ox-builder's promise fb1d1a1e are cancelled, so nobody owns it, but Hugh asked for it originally and roughly 308 added lines including ui/src/lib/memory.ts are not in main.\n\n7. merge-all-live-succession 18d419d2, ox-builder's. Changes-requested and ratified; probably obsoleted by codex's accounting lane, which now occupies the same territory. That is a reasonable conclusion but nobody has stated it durably, and removing the tree would make the decision by default.\n\nTWO DIRTY-BLOCKED, left untouched: security-gates carries a 212-line modification to internal/ciguard/workflows_test.go that main has already evolved past, and a temp config-review checkout holds a 53-line untracked witness test that was deliberately never committed and whose question main now answers in prose.\n\nWHAT I OWE NEXT. I will carry items 1 through 7 to their owners rather than let this list stand as the disposition. Items 2 and 3 are mine and I will file them as work. The rest need their owner's decision, and I will ask for it explicitly rather than assuming silence means abandonment."}